# Take your proper gander top-down, not bottom-up

You should stop reading comments on any public forum or social media.

## Against bottom-up news

1. AI has gotten good enough to superforecast.
1. AI will or already has be capable of superpersuasion.
1. [Astroturfing](https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4ng24pxkelo) is already rife on the internet. This will or already has been automated.
1. Garbage in Garbage Out
  - Protect your stimulus. You have a limited number of fucks. Choose wisely what you consume.
  - Outrage bait is an addiction, if you are addicted to it work on getting it taken away

## For top-down news

1. Reading from established publications (ideally paid) helps control some biases
  - Knowing that they're an institution you naturally critically are more skeptical and think about quality
  - Shit takes loses them money, they have a slightly more incentive.
  - You can choose to read from shops that align with your values
1. Reading the slow edition helps filter out what's more "important"
  - Ultimately though the vast majority of news is not important
1. Know what's happening locally
  - Actually have some civic duty by knowing what's happening in your community


